// Error function and complementary error function (fdlibm / FreeBSD msun s_erf.c).
//
// erf(x) = 2/sqrt(pi) * integral of exp(-t*t) from 0 to x, erfc(x) = 1 - erf(x).
// The range is split by |x|, as in fdlibm:
//   [0, 0.84375]       erf(x) = x + x*P(x*x)/Q(x*x)
//   [0.84375, 1.25]    erf(x) = erx + P(s)/Q(s) with s = |x| - 1
//   [1.25, 28]         erfc(x) = exp(-x*x - 0.5625 + R(z)/S(z)) / x, z = 1/(x*x)
// with fdlibm's minimax coefficients for the rational functions P/Q and R/S.
// Their evaluation, and that of the exponential, is carried out in
// double-double precision here (the double evaluation costs up to 2 ulp in
// erfc, which loses the digits of 1 - erf(x) where that is small), so the
// results are within a fraction of an ulp of the exact value, up to the
// 2**-58 accuracy of the approximations. erfc keeps full relative accuracy for
// large x, where erf is 1 to working precision.
//
// Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. Developed
// at SunPro, a Sun Microsystems, Inc. business. Permission to use, copy,
// modify, and distribute this software is freely granted, provided that this
// notice is preserved.

